    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        55,
        58
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " This library provides smart pointers and collections for managing",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        59,
        128
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " heap-allocated values.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        129,
        155
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        156,
        159
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " This library, like core, normally doesn’t need to be used directly",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        160,
        232
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " since its contents are re-exported in the [`std` crate](../std/index.html).",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        233,
        312
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " Crates that use the `#![no_std]` attribute however will typically",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        313,
        382
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " not depend on `std`, so they’d use this crate instead.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        383,
        443
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
