        444,
        447
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ## Boxed values",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        448,
        467
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        468,
        471
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " The [`Box`] type is a smart pointer type. There can only be one owner of a",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        472,
        550
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " [`Box`], and the owner can decide to mutate the contents, which live on the",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        551,
        630
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " heap.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        631,
        640
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        641,
        644
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " This type can be sent among threads efficiently as the size of a `Box` value",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        645,
        725
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " is the same as that of a pointer. Tree-like data structures are often built",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        726,
        805
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " with boxes because each node often has only one owner, the parent.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        806,
        876
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        877,
        880
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ## Reference counted pointers",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        881,
        914
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        915,
        918
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " The [`Rc`] type is a non-threadsafe reference-counted pointer type intended",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        919,
        998
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " for sharing memory within a thread. An [`Rc`] pointer wraps a type, `T`, and",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        999,
        1079
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " only allows access to `&T`, a shared reference.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1080,
        1131
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1132,
        1135
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " This type is useful when inherited mutability (such as using [`Box`]) is too",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1136,
        1216
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " constraining for an application, and is often paired with the [`Cell`] or",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1217,
        1294
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " [`RefCell`] types in order to allow mutation.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1295,
        1344
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1345,
        1348
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ## Atomically reference counted pointers",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1349,
        1393
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1394,
        1397
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " The [`Arc`] type is the threadsafe equivalent of the [`Rc`] type. It",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1398,
        1470
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " provides all the same functionality of [`Rc`], except it requires that the",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1471,
        1549
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " contained type `T` is shareable. Additionally, [`Arc<T>`][`Arc`] is itself",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1550,
        1628
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " sendable while [`Rc<T>`][`Rc`] is not.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1629,
        1671
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1672,
        1675
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " This type allows for shared access to the contained data, and is often",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1676,
        1750
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " paired with synchronization primitives such as mutexes to allow mutation of",
      "path": "doc",
